    "description": "One checkbox on Deal. When checked, that Deal's activity doesn't count toward any of its Partner's bonus rollups.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* Exclude from Partner Bonuses — Exclude_From_Partner_Bonuses__c — Checkbox, default false\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Global exclusion for that Deal across ALL of that Partner's bonuses. Per-bonus exclusion is out of scope — Kobi: 'if you have to do some bonuses for the same partner, but other deals don't count, that might get tricky. But if we're just excluding it overall, that's pretty easy.' Joyce: 'Okay.'\n\n* Field only. The consuming rollup logic is part of the bonus model (BUILD-172) and does not exist yet.\n\n* Confirmed 2026-08-17: 'We will do Exclude from Partner Bonuses as agreed upon.' The mockup's 'Counts Toward Bonus' is NOT built — one field, not two. This is also the Deals related-list column in BUILD-132.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* Driven by a use case Lina could not confirm — Joyce recalled Catena's OLG deal shouldn't count toward Catena's bonus, Lina didn't recognise it, Joyce kept it anyway: 'I would leave that as something that could happen.' Cheap to build speculatively; worth knowing it is speculative.\n\n* Does not appear in the Aug 11 transcripts — it came out of Aug 13. Taryn's doc files it under PT-11, which is wrong; it belongs on Deal.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 13 call — Kobi proposed, Joyce accepted\n\n* Taryn doc PT-11 note (misplaced)\n\nDependencies: None\n\nOwner (proposed): TBD\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
